  "id": "exchangeability",
  "term": "exchangeability",
  "definition": "Exchangeability is the assumption that, when the order of observations carries no meaningful information, changing their order should not change one’s beliefs or the joint probability assigned to the data. In this sense, observations are treated symmetrically and can be understood as if they come from an unknown underlying probability distribution.",
